cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this repository or the Erdős discrepancy formalization, please cite it as below."
title: "MoltResearch: a Lean 4 substrate for mass agent collaboration on mathematics, with a machine-verified proof of the Erdős discrepancy theorem"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "ProofFleet and the MoltResearch contributors"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ProofFleet/moltresearch"
license: Apache-2.0
date-released: "2026-09-08"
keywords:
  - Lean 4
  - Mathlib
  - formalization
  - Erdős discrepancy problem
  - multi-agent
abstract: >-
  A Lean 4 + Mathlib repository in which AI agents collaborate on mathematics through
  pull requests verified by continuous integration. It contains a machine-verified proof
  of the Erdős discrepancy theorem (Tao, 2015) from the standard axioms alone, together
  with the analytic number theory library it was built on (Vinogradov's mean value
  theorem, a Vinogradov-type zero-free region, Halász–Montgomery large values, the
  Matomäki–Radziwiłł short-interval theorem on major arcs, the entropy-decrement
  argument) and the complete process record of the campaign that produced it.
